{"id":"chatcmpl-8e20697e-e8ad-4dd7-bec5-7b6ac4a80f72","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229078,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-driven visual question answering workflow for medical imaging where spatial ambiguity (left vs. right on a lateral projection) requires explicit disambiguation. The successful strategy combined expert consultation, targeted region-of-interest inspection, and a self-verification step before committing to an answer. The key insight is that lateral views superimpose bilateral structures, so laterality claims must be validated against orientation markers rather than assumed.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question asks about laterality (left/right) on a projection that superimposes both sides, explicitly verify orientation markers before attributing findings to one side.\",\n    \"Use targeted region-of-interest zooming to visually confirm the presence and location of small or subtle findings before answering.\",\n    \"Consult a domain-specific expert tool to independently confirm a candidate finding, then reconcile its output with visual inspection.\",\n    \"Insert a self-verification step that states the proposed answer and the specific risk/ambiguity, forcing explicit resolution of that risk before finalizing.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Always check for orientation markers (L/R) on lateral or oblique views; use ROI crops to inspect small metallic or high-contrast findings; treat expert-tool output as corroboration, not sole authority.\",\n    \"Spatial disambiguation tasks\": \"Identify which dimension is ambiguous (laterality, depth, overlap) and seek a marker or secondary cue that resolves it before answering.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification workflows\": \"Sequence tools as: expert query -> targeted visual inspection -> explicit risk-stating verification -> answer, so each step narrows uncertainty.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm orientation/laterality markers are present and consistent with the attributed side before finalizing a left/right answer.\",\n    \"State the specific ambiguity or risk in a verification step and confirm it is resolved by evidence (marker, crop, or expert output).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":558,"total_tokens":966,"completion_tokens":408,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":558},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":408}}}